  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a **binary** string `s` that includes no fewer than one `'1'`.\n\nYou have to **rearrange** the bits in such a way that the resulting binary number is the **largest odd binary number** that can be created from this combination.\n\nOutput *a string representing the largest odd binary number that can be created from the given combination.*\n\n**Note** that the resulting string **can** have leading zeros.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"010\"\nOutput: \"001\"\nExplanation: Because there is just one '1', it must be in the last position. So the answer is \"001\".\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"0101\"\nOutput: \"1001\"\nExplanation: One of the '1's must be in the last position. The maximum number that can be made with the remaining digits is \"100\". So the answer is \"1001\".\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 100`\n* `s` consists only of `'0'` and `'1'`.\n* `s` includes no fewer than one `'1'`.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
